Download not saved accessible; toast confirms no errors. To validate export content, we can capture the text by intercepting Blob before click. But the export function is inside closure; we can monkeypatch URL.createObjectURL / anchor click to capture blob text. Let's do: override HTMLAnchorElement.prototype.click temporarily; override URL.createObjectURL to read blob via FileReader? async. Simpler: override `URL.createObjectURL` to store blob, then after click use blob.text().then... But eval expects sync. Could do an async IIFE returning promise; playwright evaluates and waits.

Let's write:

```
(async () => {
 let captured=null;
 const orig=URL.createObjectURL;
 URL.createObjectURL = b => { captured=b; return orig.call(URL,b); };
 const a=HTMLAnchorElement.prototype.click;
 HTMLAnchorElement.prototype.click=function(){};
 document.querySelector('#exportRoadmapBtn').click();
 HTMLAnchorElement.prototype.click=a;
 URL.createObjectURL=orig;
 const txt= captured? await captured.text():'';
 return JSON.stringify({len:txt.length, hasReverse:txt.includes('## Ingeniería inversa'), hasGaps:..., hasRadar:..., has200: txt.includes('- [')});
})()
```

Note downloadText may use `a.click()`; good. Let's test.

